{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vqvjhh2of3oi7qgelacr56fqk5hrx4s6htuqeorofsrok3nwa6wq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration (definition of done)\n\nI built the C library exactly as `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` does (globbing `src/lib.c` into one shared lib) and ran `nm -D` on it. The library is small — 3 files, 317 lines — and exports exactly **one** public symbol:\n\n```\ncrc16          # tflac_u16 crc16(const tflac_u8 *d, tflac_u32 len, tflac_u16 crc16)\n```\n\nI checked the header for namespace/renaming macros (e.g. `#define foo NAMESPACE(foo)`) — there are none, so the linker symbol is plain `crc16`. The `tflac_crc16_tables[8][256]` array is declared `static` in the public header, so it has internal linkage and contributes **no** dynamic symbol (confirmed: it doesn't appear in `nm -D` on the C `.so`); it's reproduced as a crate-private table.\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n\n| | C `.so` | Rust `.so` |\n|---|---|---|\n| exported defined symbols | `crc16` | `crc16` |\n\n`comm -23 c.syms rust.syms` → **empty**. Full ABI coverage.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `translation/Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `translation/src/lib.rs` — `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn crc16(...)` plus the `tflac_u8/u16/u32` type aliases, with a safe `crc16_impl(&[u8], u16)` core doing the actual work\n- `translation/src/tables.rs` — the 8×256 CRC table, machine-extracted from the header (not hand-transcribed) and verified byte-for-byte against the table as the C compiler sees it (all 2048 entries match)\n\n## Fidelity notes\n\n- Arithmetic is done in `u16`, which reproduces C's promote-to-`int`-then-truncate-on-assignment behavior; the only lossy shift (`crc16 << 8`) discards exactly the bits the C truncation discards.\n- `while (len--)` in C decrements `len` even on the failing test (wrapping to `UINT32_MAX`); `len` is dead afterward, so the plain Rust loop is equivalent. Documented in a comment rather than \"fixed\".\n- Loop order and the `crc16 ^= d[0]<<8|d[1]` / table-XOR sequence are preserved verbatim; no bugs \"fixed\".\n- `len == 0` returns the seed without touching `d`, matching C (which never dereferences), and avoiding an invalid slice from a null pointer.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release` — clean, no warnings.\n- Differential harness `dlopen`s both `.so`s side by side and compares outputs: **303,372 cases, 0 mismatches**. Coverage included null pointer with `len==0`; exhaustive lengths 0–128 across 4 seeds; all-zero/all-`0xFF` buffers for every length 0–400; all 256 single-byte values × 8 seeds; 300,000 randomized cases (random length ≤1024, data, seed, and pointer offset 0–7 to vary alignment); and a 2 MiB buffer across 3 seeds. Known-answer spot checks agree: `crc16(\"123456789\", 0) = 0xfee8`, `crc16(pangram, 0xffff) = 0xa284`.\n- `c_src/` was not modified (md5sums recorded; all scratch files were kept outside `c_src/` and removed afterward).\n\nI did not delegate to sub-agents — at 317 lines total, the library fit comfortably in one pass, and every claim above comes from commands I ran and read myself."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":46524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":434,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb44bb9f-1eb9-4025-a3e9-c50eaddab549","uuid":"62a5ea0b-a895-4460-9810-ab2ad90fa96a","timestamp":"2026-08-26T20:14:58.496Z"}
